Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 21:38:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] tee: qseecom: restate why this driver exists as a case
 analysis

Framing QSEECOM as the interface for platforms too old for smcinvoke invites
the question of why the driver is needed now that QTEE is upstream, and answers
it badly: the deciding factor is which interface an application was built
against, not the age of the SoC. Set the three cases out together.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
